---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const effectiveDate = new Date('2026-08-18T00:00:00Z');
const formattedDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', {
  day: '2-digit',
  month: 'short',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
}).format(effectiveDate);
---

<Base
  title="min.one Privacy Policy — Florent Berrez"
  description="How min.one handles your daily priority and protects your privacy."
  section="utility"
  ogSlug="index"
  analytics={false}
>
  <article>
    <div class="block" style="border-bottom:none;border-image:none;padding-bottom:0">
      <span class="block-label">min.one</span>
      <div>
        <h1 class="h1">Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Your priority stays on your device. min.one has no account, backend, advertising,
          tracking or analytics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="art">
      <aside class="spec" aria-label="About this policy">
        <div>
          <span>Effective</span>
          <b><time datetime="2026-08-18">{formattedDate}</time></b>
        </div>
        <div><span>Product</span><b>min.one for iOS</b></div>
        <div><span>Operator</span><b>Florent Berrez</b></div>
        <div><span>Location</span><b>France</b></div>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>
            This policy explains how the <strong>min.one</strong> iOS app handles information.
            It applies to the app, its widgets, Live Activities, Dynamic Island surfaces and App
            Intents.
          </p>

          <h2>Information handled by the app</h2>

          <p>min.one processes a small amount of information that you provide or configure:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>the daily priority you type;</li>
            <li>its creation and completion status and timestamps;</li>
            <li>the local calendar day and time-zone identifier used for the daily reset;</li>
            <li>your widget and Live Activity appearance preferences.</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            This information is stored locally in an iOS App Group shared only by min.one and its
            widget extension. It is used to show your priority in the app and on the system surfaces
            you enable, perform completion and Undo actions, and begin each new local day empty.
          </p>

          <h2>No collection, tracking or sharing</h2>

          <p>
            min.one does not transmit your priority or app usage to Florent Berrez or to third-party
            servers. The app contains no account system, remote backend, advertising SDK, analytics
            SDK or tracking technology. Your data is not sold, rented or shared for advertising or
            profiling.
          </p>

          <p>
            The app does not request access to your contacts, photos, precise location, microphone,
            camera, health data or calendars.
          </p>

          <h2>Widgets and Live Activities</h2>

          <p>
            If you add a widget or enable Live Activities, your priority can appear on your Home
            Screen, Lock Screen or Dynamic Island. These surfaces are managed by iOS and may be
            visible to anyone who can see your device. You can remove widgets through iOS and disable
            Live Activities from min.one Settings at any time.
          </p>

          <h2>Storage, retention and deletion</h2>

          <p>
            The current priority remains in local storage for its calendar day. When min.one
            reconciles a new local day, the previous record is removed rather than carried forward.
            Appearance preferences remain until you change them or remove the app.
          </p>

          <p>
            You can clear the current priority by choosing <strong>Replace</strong> and leaving the
            new entry empty, or delete the app to remove its local app container. Copies may remain
            in device or iCloud backups according to your Apple backup settings and Apple's retention
            practices. min.one cannot access or delete those backups for you.
          </p>

          <h2>Apple services</h2>

          <p>
            iOS, the App Store, iCloud, device backups and optional diagnostics are Apple services.
            Apple may process information independently under its own
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.
            min.one does not receive your priority through those services.
          </p>

          <h2>When you contact support</h2>

          <p>
            If you email support, Florent Berrez receives the address, message and any information
            you choose to include. It is used only to answer your request, maintain necessary support
            records and meet legal obligations. It is not used for advertising and is deleted when it
            is no longer reasonably needed. Do not include your daily priority unless it is necessary
            to explain the issue.
          </p>

          <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>

          <p>
            Because app content is not sent to a server, Florent Berrez cannot view, export or delete
            it remotely. You control it directly on your device. For questions about this policy or a
            request concerning a support email, contact
            <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hi@fberrez.co">hi@fberrez.co</a><!--email_on-->.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>

          <p>
            This page will be updated if min.one's data practices change. The effective date above
            will change at the same time, and the app's App Store privacy disclosures will be updated
            when required.
          </p>
        </div>

        <footer class="art-foot">
          <a href="/">← Index</a>
          <span>Florent Berrez · France</span>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
